# AI review pipeline

Engineering process, not a product feature. Website review is a **Perception Engine** module — see `.cursor/rules/perception-engine.mdc` and `docs/perception/`.

## Artifacts are observations

Files under `docs/ai-review/runs/` record **what was seen**. They are **not** implementation instructions, tickets, or authorised work. **artifact ≠ build order.**

- Do not treat run files as a build checklist or patch order.
- Do not invent unverified metrics (Law 1).
- Optional `candidates` are idea labels only — not tasks.
- Prefer citing stable observation IDs (e.g. `library.live-snapshot`) and `origin` in plans.

## What you may do

- Read `docs/ai-review/` and Stage 1 portal docs.
- Run `npm run ai-review` (fixture) or `npm run ai-review:prod` when env credentials are set (read-only).
- From runs with `status: accepted_for_planning`, draft a **plan** that cites the artifact id and observation IDs.
- The plan is new work product; the artifact did not prescribe the design.

## What you must not do

- Implement, commit, PR, migrate, or deploy from an artifact alone.
- Put credentials or secrets into run files.
- Treat artifacts as Masterplan / AGENTS authority.
- Start coding until the owner explicitly approves implementation (e.g. “authorise”, “implement the plan”, “proceed”).

## Stage 1 reminder

Fixture portal lives only under `/__e2e__/ai-review` with `VITE_E2E_FIXTURES=on`. Never ship fixtures to production.
